ue) \/\/ prints 55 after retry on NetworkError.timeout","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"aside","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Not every ","type":"text"},{"code":"AsyncSequence","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" can be retried, for this to work the sequence has to implement an iterator that doesn’t preserve state across various creations.","type":"text"}]}],"name":"Important","style":"important"},{"type":"aside","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":""},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AsyncStream"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AsyncThrowingStream"},{"type":"text","text":" are notable sequences which cannot be retried on their own."}]}],"name":"Note","style":"note"}],"kind":"content"}],"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent","doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/AsyncSequences","doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/AsyncSequences\/RetryOn"]]},"metadata":{"extendedModule":"_Concurrency","roleHeading":"Instance Method","modules":[{"relatedModules":["_Concurrency"],"name":"Afluent"}],"title":"retry(_:on:)","conformance":{"conformancePrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Conforms when"}],"availabilityPrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Available when"}],"constraints":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self"},{"type":"text","text":" conforms to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sendable"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Element"},{"type":"text","text":" conforms to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sendable"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},"role":"symbol","remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Afluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Afluent\/SequenceOperators\/RetrySequence.swift#L491","fileName":"RetrySequence.swift"},"externalID":"s:Sci7Afluents8SendableRzsAB7ElementRpzrlE5retry_2onAA14AsyncSequencesO11RetryOnCastCy_xqd__AA0H15ByCountStrategyCGSu_qd__mts5ErrorRd__lF::SYNTHESIZED::s:7Afluent14AsyncSequencesO7RetryOnC","symbolK